\subsection{Method \code{mars_fit()}}{
Fit a MARS regression model (requires \pkg{earth})

Multivariate Adaptive Regression Splines (MARS) build a piecewise
regression by searching hinge functions and their products. This
method wraps \code{\link[earth:earth]{earth::earth()}} and surfaces the selected terms, the
generalized R-squared, and the GCV statistic.
\subsection{Usage}{
\if{html}{\out{<div class="r">}}\preformatted{RegressionAnalyzer$mars_fit(
  formula,
  data,
  degree = 1,
  nk = NULL,
  thresh = 0.001,
  pmethod = "backward",
  trace = FALSE,
  subset = NULL,
  na.action = stats::na.omit
)}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}
}

\subsection{Arguments}{
\if{html}{\out{<div class="arguments">}}
\describe{
\item{\code{formula}}{A model formula (response on left, predictors on right).}

\item{\code{data}}{A data frame.}

\item{\code{degree}}{Maximum interaction degree (default 1, additive MARS).}

\item{\code{nk}}{Maximum number of model terms. NULL lets earth auto-select.}

\item{\code{thresh}}{Forward step threshold. Default uses earth's default.}

\item{\code{pmethod}}{Pruning method. Default "backward".}

\item{\code{trace}}{Logical; print earth progress.}

\item{\code{subset}}{Optional subset expression.}

\item{\code{na.action}}{NA handling.}
}
\if{html}{\out{</div>}}
}
